<section class="panel" id="verify">
  <h2>Verify your download</h2>
  <p class="muted">
    Every release carries <code>SHA256SUMS</code>, signed with the Mortar packages key, and a GitHub build
    provenance attestation for each file. With the downloaded file in the current folder:
  </p>
  <div data-for="windows">
    <p class="muted">In PowerShell. <code>gpg</code> comes with <a href="https://gpg4win.org/">Gpg4win</a>, <code>gh</code> is the <a href="https://cli.github.com/">GitHub CLI</a>.</p>
    <pre><code>$f = '<span class="vfile">mortar-amd64-installer.exe</span>'
$base = 'https://github.com/Rethunk-Tech/mortar/releases/latest/download'
Invoke-WebRequest "$base/SHA256SUMS" -OutFile SHA256SUMS
Invoke-WebRequest "$base/SHA256SUMS.asc" -OutFile SHA256SUMS.asc
Invoke-WebRequest https://mortar.rethunk.tech/packages/mortar-archive-keyring.asc -OutFile mortar.asc
gpg --import mortar.asc
gpg --verify SHA256SUMS.asc SHA256SUMS
$want = (Select-String -Path SHA256SUMS -Pattern "  $([regex]::Escape($f))$").Line.Split(' ')[0]
if ((Get-FileHash $f).Hash -eq $want) { 'OK' } else { 'MISMATCH' }
gh attestation verify $f --repo Rethunk-Tech/mortar</code></pre>
  </div>
  <div data-for="linux">
    <p class="muted">In a terminal.</p>
    <pre><code>f=<span class="vfile">mortar-linux-x86_64.AppImage</span>
curl -fsSLO https://github.com/Rethunk-Tech/mortar/releases/latest/download/SHA256SUMS
curl -fsSLO https://github.com/Rethunk-Tech/mortar/releases/latest/download/SHA256SUMS.asc
curl -fsSL https://mortar.rethunk.tech/packages/mortar-archive-keyring.asc | gpg --import
gpg --verify SHA256SUMS.asc SHA256SUMS
grep "  $f\$" SHA256SUMS | sha256sum --check
gh attestation verify "$f" --repo Rethunk-Tech/mortar</code></pre>
  </div>
  <p class="fingerprint">
    One key, “Mortar packages &lt;opensource@rethunk.tech&gt;”, signs every release's <code>SHA256SUMS</code> and
    the apt, dnf, pacman and Flatpak repositories, so every download checks against the same fingerprint:
    <code>D8B1 C4C2 05C5 FB36 33CB 8B99 00B7 5959 B637 DCB5</code>.
    <a href="/packages/">Repository details</a> · <a href="/code-signing/">Code signing policy</a>
  </p>
</section>


